# 🔢 Operators in Go

Operators are special symbols used to perform operations on variables and values.

---

# 1. Arithmetic Operators

| Operator | Meaning        |
| -------- | -------------- |
| +        | Addition       |
| -        | Subtraction    |
| *        | Multiplication |
| /        | Division       |
| %        | Modulus        |

---

## Example

### Problem:

Calculate the sum of two numbers.

```go
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
    a := 20
    b := 10

    fmt.Println("Addition =", a+b)
    fmt.Println("Subtraction =", a-b)
    fmt.Println("Multiplication =", a*b)
    fmt.Println("Division =", a/b)
    fmt.Println("Remainder =", a%b)
}
```

### Output

```text
Addition = 30
Subtraction = 10
Multiplication = 200
Division = 2
Remainder = 0
```

---

# 2. Assignment Operators

| Operator | Example |
| -------- | ------- |
| =        | a = 10  |
| +=       | a += 5  |
| -=       | a -= 5  |
| *=       | a *= 5  |
| /=       | a /= 5  |
| %=       | a %= 5  |

---

## Example

```go
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
    x := 10

    x += 5

    fmt.Println(x)
}
```

### Output

```text
15
```

---

# 3. Comparison Operators

Used to compare two values.

| Operator | Meaning               |
| -------- | --------------------- |
| ==       | Equal to              |
| !=       | Not Equal             |
| >        | Greater Than          |
| <        | Less Than             |
| >=       | Greater Than or Equal |
| <=       | Less Than or Equal    |

---

## Example

### Problem:

Check whether two marks are equal.

```go
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
    marks1 := 90
    marks2 := 90

    fmt.Println(marks1 == marks2)
}
```

### Output

```text
true
```

---

# 4. Logical Operators

| Operator | Meaning     |   |            |
| -------- | ----------- | - | ---------- |
| &&       | Logical AND |   |            |
|          |             |   | Logical OR |
| !        | Logical NOT |   |            |

---

## Example

### Problem:

Check if a student passed both subjects.

```go
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
    math := true
    science := true

    fmt.Println(math && science)
}
```

### Output

```text
true
```

---

# 5. Increment and Decrement Operators

```go
x++
x--
```

## Example

```go
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
    x := 10

    x++

    fmt.Println(x)
}
```

### Output

```text
11
```

